Dear Edward,

I=E2=80=99m sending the revised Chapter 2, =E2=80=9CDues and participation=E2=
=80=9D (LHT-20250212-CHP-001 v1.1), and my separate response to all eleven po=
ints in ASP-2025-REV-001, ahead of tomorrow=E2=80=99s deadline. I=E2=80=99ve =
made changes to the text or notes for nine of the points. The response gives =
the relevant passages and notes in the revised Word file.

For R10, comparing visit rates would require a record of visits that can be l=
inked to members=E2=80=99 payment status over the same period, as well as the=
 number of members eligible to visit in each group. I=E2=80=99ve kept =C2=A76=
 to what the papers establish about the terms of access. For R11, the address=
 on the forwarding copy gives me a spelling to index. I would need a contempo=
rary record locating Val d=E2=80=99Erne and evidence of the intervening hando=
vers before I could draw the route. The response sets out both gaps, and =C2=
=A75 gives the spelling and the leaf and line reference.

Please pass on my thanks to the reader. The request to give the preceding per=
mission on f. 186r helped me make clear why reading in the room and borrowing=
 a book had to be discussed separately.

Best wishes,
Judith

